Local integration in vc-attention:
- Independent sageattention_local Python package and Torch operator namespaces.
- Independent sageattention-local distribution, version 2.2.0+vc27.1.
- Hopper-only build of the baseline _qattn_sm90 and _fused CUDA extensions.
- Distinct name for the SM90 fake implementation, avoiding shadowing the CUDA callable.
- Remove the unused CUDAContext.h include in fused.cu to avoid unnecessary cuSPARSE headers.
- Build provenance, validation and same-process comparison scripts.
Baseline CUDA/C++ kernel bodies and Triton kernel source content are unchanged;
the one CUDA include edit is recorded in UPSTREAM.json.

Sage+VC experiment, separate entry sageattn_vc and extension _vc_sm90:
- csrc/vc/vc_sm90.cu derives from the above upstream Hopper kernel and retains its license header.
- Replaces probability conversion with optional VC ExpCast; adds per-block V scale and mean restoration.
- Adds native V residual quantization, GPU clustering orchestration, and Python API/diagnostic oracle.
- Keeps Sage INT8 QK: this hybrid is not a full VC-Attention paper reproduction.
- vc4 pairs FP8 decode and V metadata loads, and overlaps next-V TMA with mean restoration.
- vc5 shortens the ExpCast maximum reduction and uses FMA for V mean restoration; retains vc4 as a selectable comparison kernel.
- vc6-vc8 add shared channel V scales, streamed ExpCast encoding/reduction and compact D128 PV fragments.
- vc9 adds fused CUDA Lloyd assignment/partial statistics, retaining stable sorting and the selectable legacy clustering path.
- vc10 changes only the ExpCast-without-V-smoothing core: independent exact tile sums and PV-overlapped history scaling; FP8 encoding is unchanged, FP32 history-add rounding can differ. Prior vc9 kernels remain selectable.
- vc11-vc15 schedule and simplify the ExpCast encoding/reduction pipeline, including paired conversion and four-byte packing. Historical paths remain selectable.
- vc16 adds csrc/vc/sage_layout.cuh, also derived from the pinned upstream Hopper kernel with its license retained. It exposes sum/pack, next-V prefetch and ExpCast history schedules independently; default remains vc15.
- vc17 adds probability_variants.cuh: selectable fragment batch sizes, FP32 sum chains and direct positive-E4M3 decoding on the vc16 body. Historical helpers remain unchanged; default remains vc15.
- vc18-vc24 retain selectable register, buffering, history, integer-max and probability-encoding experiments. The reported vc22_both path remains the measured experimental baseline.
- vc25 adds deferred_mass.cuh and source scheduling candidates on vc22: preserve completed FP8 P for denominator reduction during the next QK, with neutral initial state and final masked-tile drain. Source schedules may compile identically; no Hopper speed claim from local checks. Default remains vc15.
Modified and new experiment files are recorded separately in UPSTREAM.json.

vc27 FP8 QK experiment, separate entry sageattn_vc_fp8:
- Adds block-scaled E4M3 Q/K with native FP32 K centering and unchanged global FP8 V.
- fp8_qk_mma.cuh derives from the pinned csrc/wgmma.cuh with its Apache-2.0 header retained.
- Extends the local sage_layout template with an opt-in FP8 shared/shared QK instruction;
  no upstream baseline kernel is changed. FP32 probability max and optional ExpCast remain fused.
- No Hadamard, V grouping/smoothing or denoising-step scheduling in this first FP8 entry.
- vc27.1 adds global_values.cuh, derived from the pinned fused.cu MeanScaleKernel,
  retaining its Apache-2.0 notice. The FP8 entry handles zero V channels inside the
  existing quantization pass; nonzero math and baseline kernel sources are unchanged.
